# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values for your build.
#
# Expo only exposes variables prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ to the app bundle — do not
# rename this or the app won't pick it up. It's baked into the build at build
# time, not read at runtime, so a live build needs the live URL set here
# before running `eas build`.

# The vendor API base URL. Leave unset for local development and the app
# falls back to the live site automatically (see src/api/client.ts). Point
# this at your local Laravel server while developing against it, e.g.
# http://localhost:8000/api/v1/vendor or http://<your-machine-ip>:8011/api/v1/vendor
# (a phone or simulator on the same network can't reach "localhost" — use the
# machine's LAN IP instead).
#
# For a live/production build, set this to the real site:
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://11done.co.uk/api/v1/vendor
